  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Nevada has received $2.9B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Award activity includes 19,118 contracts with an average award size of $151K, and obligations fell 28.4% year over year. Historically, obligations rose from $3.1B in FY21 to $4B in both FY24 and FY25 before moving to $2.9B in FY26. The Department of Defense obligated $1.1B and the Department of Energy obligated $1B in Nevada during FY2026 to date. Facilities Support Services is the largest industry by obligations at $1B, followed by Engineering Services at $560M and Automobile Manufacturing at $433M. At the vendor level, MISSION SUPPORT & TEST SERVICES LLC received $953M, and FLEET VEHICLE SOURCE INC received $433M. The General Services Administration obligated $499M, while the Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $85.1M. These figures reflect contract obligations only and represent partial fiscal year totals for FY2026 to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has Nevada’s federal contracting trended recently?",
        "body": "Obligations rose from $3.1B in FY21 to $4B in FY24 and remained $4B in FY25, then moved to $2.9B in FY26. Award count in FY2026 to date is 19,118 with an average award size of $151K. Year over year, obligations fell 28.4%."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the biggest buyers and suppliers in Nevada right now?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $1.1B and the Department of Energy obligated $1B in FY2026 to date. MISSION SUPPORT & TEST SERVICES LLC received $953M and FLEET VEHICLE SOURCE INC received $433M. Facilities Support Services accounted for $1B in obligations and Engineering Services accounted for $560M."
      }
    ]
  },
